sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-06> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Ten days after transient octanol exposure, regenerated G. dorotocephala show more distinct isopotential (membrane-voltage) regions by DiBAC dye imaging than controls, and the number of isopotential regions returns to the wild-type level after 30 days of morphological remodeling.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Octanol-treated worms show more isopotential regions, which return to normal by 30 days";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Emmons-Bell M, Durant F, Hammelman J, Bessonov N, Volpert V, Morokuma J, Pinet K, Adams DS, Pietak A, Lobo D, Levin M, “Gap Junctional Blockade Stochastically Induces Different Species-Specific Head Anatomies in Genetically Wild-Type Girardia dorotocephala Flatworms”, International journal of molecular sciences (2015), doi:10.3390/ijms161126065; section “2. Results › 2.6. Patterns of Endogenous Relative Membrane Potential Are Altered in GJ-Perturbed Worms”. Scope: Whole-body DiBAC4(3) voltage-dye images of octanol-treated and control G. dorotocephala at 10 and 30 days"
}
